  "result": "I wrote the rule and its four test scenarios for `NRS_484B_785_1a`, and the gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of the 6 runs used).\n\n**The rule:**\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is an electric scooter (`ru_electric_scooter`).\n- **When it applies:** the scooter's footprint overlaps a roadway or a bicycle lane or path (`rel_occupies`). Each region check is limited to that kind of region and tied to the scooter.\n- **The duty:** the scooter's `kin_speed` is at most `Units.mph 15`, which is 6.7056 m/s and is the law's own figure.\n- **Not written:** the ordinance exception (s1) and \"may be operated\" (s3) stay as the blueprint's residues; it says neither changes the speed bound. I added no narrowings, because the blueprint leaves no choice open.\n\n**The scenarios:** a roadway, a bicycle lane and a sidewalk lie side by side. In each one the scooter rides east for 3 instants, 1 s apart.\n\n| Scenario | Scooter | Expected verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | on the roadway at 8 m/s | violated |\n| permit | in the bicycle lane at 5 m/s | compliant |\n| idle | on the sidewalk at 8 m/s, touching neither the roadway nor the bicycle lane | not applicable |\n| blind | on the roadway, speed not observed | unknown |\n\nFiles changed:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_785_1a.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_785_1a.lean`\n- `task_result.md` (in the working directory)",
